  "id": "Compound::DB01193 - Gene::154",
  "verbalization": "Acebutolol is associated with Adrb2 through a series of interconnected pathways that involve beta-adrenergic antagonism. The evidence suggests that Acebutolol may influence Adrb2 through its interaction with beta-adrenergic receptors, as it is linked to short-term memory loss, which is mediated by penbutolol or metoprolol. Both penbutolol and metoprolol bind to Adrb2, indicating a potential mechanism by which Acebutolol could exert its effects on Adrb2. The presence of a common ancestor, Acebutolol and metoprolol, both belonging to the Beta-Adrenergic Antagonist class, further supports this relationship. The evidence is consistent with a role for Acebutolol in modulating Adrb2 activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further research is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Acebutolol in Adrb2 regulation.",
